# Flora math verification

When changing or reviewing Chao1, Mann–Kendall, Pearson r, Shannon/Simpson, Jaccard/Sørensen, EOO/AOO, or KDE bandwidth, use the **flora-math** MCP (SciPy/NumPy references) instead of trusting mental arithmetic.

1. Read resource `flora-math://algorithms` if unsure which tool maps to which JS file.
2. Call the matching `*_reference` tool with the same fixture the JS code uses.
3. Call `compare_js_to_reference` and report mismatches.
4. EOO area may differ slightly: JS is Turf geodesic, MCP is local km hull.
5. Mann–Kendall tau in JS is Kendall-a (`S / C(n,2)`); SciPy `kendalltau` variant b can differ with ties.
